+def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
+    """
+    Reconstruct the original framed-source beam dynamics, but render only the emitted ray layer.
+
+    Input structure:
+    - The most common color is background, and every source is a monochrome 2x2 block inside a 4x4 frame.
+    - Each frame has one or more structural background gaps on its border, which define beam launch sites.
+
+    Rule:
+    - Each structural gap emits the inner block color in the outward direction implied by its side or corner.
+    - Beam motion, stopping conditions, 90-degree collision turns, 45-degree zigzag merges, and diagonal
+      geometric crossing behavior are unchanged from the base task.
+    - The frame still blocks motion during simulation because the solver reads occupancy from the input grid,
+      but the returned canvas starts blank, so every frame pixel and every inner source pixel disappear.
+
+    Key insight:
+    - The fused variant changes visibility, not physics: infer the same emission-and-collision system from
+      the input sources, then keep only the post-emission traces so the output is a pure record of ray travel.
