    12	# Design analysis for the combo variant
    13	# -------------------------------------
    14	# a) Concrete behavior and trace:
    15	#    - Input remains the original family: 4x4 shared-color frames surround monochrome 2x2 blocks,
    16	#      and 1-4 structural border gaps seed outward rays.
    17	#    - Original task: the output preserves the frame and source block, then overlays the emitted rays.
    18	#    - D13 alone: simulate exactly the same rays, then erase the source frame/block from the output.
    19	#    - D12 alone: return only the ray layer on a blank background canvas.
    20	#    - Combined rule: after emission the source object is consumed, and the final raster keeps only
    21	#      ray pixels. In a concrete example, a red block with one NE gap still emits the same red beam
    22	#      and participates in the same collisions, but the green frame and red 2x2 seed vanish entirely.
    23	#      The gap cell remains colored because it is the first ray pixel, not part of the erased source.
    24	# b) Complexity calibration:
    25	#    - The beam physics, collision taxonomy, gap combinatorics, block-count range, and color choices
    26	#      stay unchanged, so the task does not collapse into a simple one-line extrapolation problem.
    27	#    - The visual difference is still strong: each source removes 12-15 non-background pixels from
    28	#      the output while preserving only the dynamically generated trajectories.
    29	# c) Implicit-assumption audit:
    30	#    - The base solver assumed `out = g.copy()` because static sources survived. That assumption no
    31	#      longer holds; `out` must start as a pure background canvas.
    32	#    - Detection of frames, colors, and gaps must continue to read `g`, because the input still
    33	#      contains intact sources and the solver must infer emission from them.
    34	#    - Motion legality must also keep reading `g`, not `out`; otherwise erased frames would stop
    35	#      behaving as obstacles and the combo would accidentally alter beam physics in addition to output.
    36	#    - Beam seeds are still required to be background in the input, so spawning onto a blank `out`
    37	#      is safe and keeps the first visible pixel at the gap.
    38	# d) Placement legality:
    39	#    - Generator keeps the original 4x4 frame footprint, in-bounds placement margin, and frame-frame
